<?php
/**
 * 8E — Le domande frequenti in inglese (/en, /en/questions): stessi id di Faq::tutte(), così le ancore
 * (#faq-…, /en/questions#…) funzionano nelle due lingue. Le parti calcolate (prezzi del Portfolio,
 * percentuali di «Bring a friend») arrivano in $v da Faq::tutte('en').
 * @param array $v ['prima' => «€117», 'tiers' => «…», 'unica' => «€60», 'max_q' => 50, 'amico' => 5, 'passo' => 5, 'massimo' => 50, 'amici' => 10]
 * @return array<string,array{0:string,1:string}> id => [domanda, risposta]
 */
return function (array $v): array {
    return [
        'prova' => ['Can I try it before I pay?', 'Yes. You create your account with no credit card, build your guide and preview it on your phone exactly as your guests will see it. You only pay when you decide to publish it.'],
        'app' => ['Do guests need an app?', 'No. The guide opens in the phone\'s browser, from a link or a QR code. Guests don\'t download anything, and neither do you: the dashboard works on a computer and on a phone.'],
        'tempo' => ['How long does it take to set up?', 'To get started all you need is the name of your property and the town. Check-in and Wi-Fi take a few minutes; you add the rest whenever you like, one section at a time. Everything saves as you type.'],
        'lingue' => ['Which languages can guests read it in?', 'With Essential, two languages: yours and one of your choice. With Plus and Portfolio, six: yours, the others among Italian, English, French, German and Spanish, plus one extra language of your choice among Dutch, European Portuguese, Brazilian Portuguese, Polish, Russian, Chinese, Japanese, Swedish, Danish and Czech. The first time they open the guide, guests choose their language, with their phone\'s language at the top. With Essential you write the translations yourself, next to the original text; with Plus and Portfolio you get translations suggested by the automatic translator, you approve them, included in the plan within a yearly limit; section titles, categories and place labels are already translated (for Russian, Chinese, Japanese, Swedish, Danish and Czech the guide\'s buttons are in English).'],
        'lingua-principale' => ['Can I write the guide in another language?', 'Yes, in any language you like. In Settings, under "Which language do you write the guide in?", Italian is the default, but you can choose English, German, Russian, Brazilian Portuguese or any of the others: it is the language of your texts and the one suggested translations start from. With Essential you have your language and a second one of your choice. With Plus and Portfolio, if you write in one of the five base languages you also get the others plus one extra language; if you write in another language, it takes the place of the extra language and you get all five base languages. The guide\'s buttons and titles are translated into the base languages and into Dutch, Portuguese and Polish; for the other languages guests read them in English. The dashboard stays in Italian. If you change the language later, the texts you have already written stay in the language you wrote them in and become a translation.'],
        'traduzioni' => ['Do you translate it for me?', 'With Plus and Portfolio you get translations suggested by the automatic translator (Amazon Translate): you approve them, included in the plan within a yearly character limit shown in the dashboard. On each language page you tap "Translate" next to a field, or "Translate all missing fields", and check the suggestions one by one: guests only see the ones you approve. They are machine translations: for important texts, have a native speaker read them.'],
        // 10 · «Ask the guide»
        'assistente' => ['What is "Ask the guide"?', 'An assistant inside the guest guide. The guest types a question in their language and the assistant answers with the information you wrote: times, Wi-Fi, parking, rules, surroundings. Under every answer is the section of the guide it comes from. It is included in the Plus and Portfolio plans.'],
        'assistente-inventa' => ['Can it make answers up?', 'It only answers with what is in the guide. If the guide doesn\'t say, it says so clearly and sends the guest to your contacts (WhatsApp or phone). Under the chat it always says that answers are automatic. In the dashboard you see the unanswered questions: add the information and next time it answers by itself.'],
        'assistente-quante' => ['How many questions does it include?', 'Up to ' . number_format((int) $v['domande']) . ' questions a month for each property, more than a normal holiday home receives. If you use them up in a month, the assistant stops until the next month and the guide stays as always; we warn you at 80%.'],
        'assistente-privacy' => ['What about guests\' privacy?', 'Questions are not linked to a person: no name, no account, no cookies. To answer, the question and the guide\'s text go to an artificial-intelligence provider (Anthropic) which, under its terms, does not use them to train its models; it is listed in the privacy policy. The conversation disappears when the guest closes the page; the question is kept for 12 months, anonymous, so you can see what the guide is missing.'],
        'assistente-spegnere' => ['Can I turn it off?', 'Yes, for each guide, from Settings → Ask the guide. You can also choose whether to show your contacts when it cannot answer.'],
        'assistente-lingue' => ['Which languages does it answer in?', 'The language the guest writes in, even if the guide is not translated into it: it reads your information in Italian and answers in German, Dutch, Polish… The guide\'s languages remain the ones you publish.'],
        'traduzioni-suggerite' => ['Do suggested translations change what I have already written?', 'No. Translations are only suggested where they are missing: what you have translated yourself is never touched. If you later change the original text, the suggestion needs redoing, and we tell you.'],
        'sezione-libera' => ['Can I add a section of my own?', 'Yes. Besides the ready-made sections there is the "Free section" (you choose the title, the icon and the text), one per guide, in every plan. With Essential it counts as one of the ' . $v['sez_ess'] . ' extra sections; with Plus and Portfolio it is included like the others.'],
        'recensioni' => ['How do I ask guests for a review?', 'In QR & Link you will find the end-of-stay message, ready to copy in the guest\'s language: send it on WhatsApp or in the Booking.com or Airbnb chat. The link opens a page where the guest gives a rating from 1 to 5. Guests who give 5 stars see buttons for the platforms you have ticked in Settings ("Which platforms is your property on?"): we prepare the links. With 1 to 4 stars, guests can write to you on WhatsApp to tell you what to improve.'],
        'qr' => ['Can I change the texts after printing the QR code?', 'Yes, whenever you like. The QR code never changes, even when you edit the guide: you publish the new version and anyone scanning the printed QR code sees it straight away. It stays valid as long as your subscription is active.'],
        'piu-strutture' => ['I have more than one property: how does it work?', 'With Portfolio you manage them all from the same account: each one has its own guide, QR code and statistics. Sections that apply to all of them, like restaurants or house rules, you write once and copy to the others.'],
        'costo-portfolio' => ['How much does each property cost with Portfolio?', 'The first one costs ' . $v['prima'] . '; '
            . ($v['tiers'] !== '' ? 'after that, each additional property costs less, in tiers: ' . $v['tiers'] : 'each additional property costs ' . $v['unica'] . ', up to ' . $v['max_q'] . ' properties (for more, write to us)')
            . '. Annual prices, excluding VAT. In the price list you choose how many properties you need and see the total and the average cost of each; inside the dashboard you will find the breakdown property by property.'],
        'oltre-portfolio' => ['More than ' . $v['max_q'] . ' properties?', 'Beyond ' . $v['max_q'] . ' properties we make you a tailored offer: ask for a quote from the price list. '
            . 'We email you a link with the agreed annual price for all your properties; you accept it and pay on Stripe, like our other plans. The same price applies at renewal. '
            . 'The discounts of the referral programme and «Review with a discount» do not apply automatically to tailored offers: we review them with you before each renewal.'],
        'bnb-camere' => ['I run a B&B, guesthouse or farm stay with several rooms: do I need several guides?', 'No. Several rooms at the same address and with the same CIN (Italy\'s national property code) are one property: one guide is enough. If the rooms have different Wi-Fi networks, add a row for each area in the Wi-Fi section.'],
        'piu-case' => ['Can I put several houses in one guide?', 'No. A guide corresponds to one rental unit, with its own address and CIN, which is needed to publish and cannot appear on two guides. For several houses or apartments there is Portfolio: each property has its own guide, and from the second one on it costs less.'],
        'google' => ['Can people find my guide on Google?', 'No, and that is deliberate, for your privacy and your guests\'. The guide contains the address of the house, how to get in, the Wi-Fi and your contact details: useful to people staying there, not to anyone searching online. That is why it doesn\'t appear on Google or other search engines, and AI assistants like ChatGPT don\'t read it: only people with the link or the QR code can open it. The MyHouse Welcome pages that explain the service, on the other hand, are found as usual.'],
        'codice-porta' => ['Can I put the door code in the guide?', 'We advise against it. The guide opens from a link, with no password: anyone with the link can read it, and a link can be forwarded. A code written there would stay readable even after the guest has left, putting the house and the privacy of the next guests at risk. So if you write a code for doors, key boxes, safes or alarms, the platform warns you and asks you to confirm, before publishing, that you do so at your own risk. In the guide, explain how to get in and where the keys are; give the code to the guest in person or privately, shortly before arrival.'],
        'fattura' => ['Do I get an invoice?', 'Yes. Before your first payment you enter your billing details once: for a company or freelancer, VAT number and SDI code or certified email (PEC); for a private person, the tax code is enough. The electronic invoice reaches you by email from Adamo, with a courtesy PDF copy; the original is in your tax drawer (cassetto fiscale) or at your recipient code / PEC. Under Account & Billing → "Payments and invoices" you find every payment with its code.'],
        'codice-partner' => ['I have a partner code: what does it give me?', 'A partner code (for example PM-ROSSI) comes from a property manager or an agency working with us. Enter it in the "Have a code?" field before paying, or arrive from their link: you get their discount on the first year (it adds up with a friend\'s invitation; with a discount code the higher one applies; it does not apply with a gift code). We pay the partner a commission: you pay nothing more, and they only see the property name and town, the plan and the dates, never your email or your payments.'],
        'cambio-piano' => ['Can I change plan later?', 'Yes, whenever you like, from Account & Billing → "Change plan". If you upgrade (from Essential to Plus, from Plus to Portfolio, or add properties to Portfolio) you only pay today the difference for the days left until renewal, and the new plan applies as soon as the payment is confirmed. The renewal date doesn\'t change. If you downgrade, you pay nothing today: the change starts at renewal and until then you stay on the plan you have already paid for.'],
        'scendere-piano' => ['Do I lose anything if I downgrade?', 'Nothing is deleted. Before confirming you choose which sections to keep and, with Portfolio, which properties to archive, and you see the list of what the guide will no longer show (for example languages beyond yours and a second one). Whatever the new plan doesn\'t include stays saved and comes back as soon as you upgrade again. You can cancel the change until the day before renewal.'],
        'porta-amico' => ['How does "Bring a friend" work?', 'Once your guide is published, under "Invite a friend" you will find your personal link. Anyone who signs up from that link gets ' . $v['amico'] . '% off their first year. For every friend who pays for their subscription, your next renewal costs ' . $v['passo'] . '% less: with ' . $v['amici'] . ' friends you reach ' . $v['massimo'] . '%. The discount is applied automatically to your renewal invoice, with no codes to enter.' . ($v['giudizio'] ? ' It is a different programme from "Review with a discount", which gives another ' . $v['giudizio'] . '%: the two add up, together up to ' . $v['totale'] . '% off your next renewal.' : '')],
        'amico-quando' => ['When does a friend count, and what happens after renewal?', 'A friend counts when they pay for their first subscription, with billing details different from yours (another VAT number or tax code). While they have only signed up, they show as "pending". The discount applies to your next renewal: after that, the count starts again from zero and new friends count towards the following year. Beyond ' . $v['amici'] . ' friends the discount doesn\'t grow. If you turn off automatic renewal, the discount isn\'t used: it doesn\'t become a refund.'],
        'campione' => ['What is the template guide?', \MHW\TestiSito::testoSemplice('campione.testo')],
        'campione-copia' => ['What is copied and what is not?', 'Copied (and updated): ' . implode('; ', array_filter(array_map(fn($r) => trim((string) preg_replace('/\*\*(.+?)\*\*/s', '$1', $r)), explode("\n", \MHW\TestiSito::get('campione.si'))))) . '. Never copied: ' . implode('; ', array_filter(array_map('trim', explode("\n", \MHW\TestiSito::get('campione.no'))))) . '. Nothing is copied by itself: you confirm, section by section.'],
        'attivazione' => ['When do automatic translation and the template guide switch on?', \MHW\TestiSito::testoSemplice('attivazione.spiegone')],
        'giudizio-sconto' => ['What is the "Review with a discount" programme?', 'With a single checkbox, at checkout or from your dashboard (Settings → Review with a discount), you join and commit to leaving us a rating from 1 to 5 with a comment. The ' . $v['giudizio'] . '% discount applies only once: on the first year if you join at checkout (or before your first payment); if you join later, on the following renewal, provided you have left the review by then (otherwise on the first renewal after the review). It is not repeated on later renewals. On the renewal it adds up with invitations into a single percentage on the list price (up to ' . $v['totale'] . '%); it does not add up with discount codes (the higher one applies). With a gift code you can join during the free months too: the discount applies from the first renewal after the first payment. We ask for the review 30 days after publishing and, if you joined after paying, again one month before renewal. The discount does not depend on the rating: it applies even with one star. If you do not join, we publish nothing about you.'],
        'omaggio' => ['I have a gift code: do the discounts apply too?', 'Yes, after the first payment. With a gift code the first months are free; at the end the subscription starts at the full price of the plan, with notices 30 and 7 days before. During the free months the discount of an invitation you received does not apply, but you can already join "Review with a discount" and invite friends. From the first renewal after the first payment you get all the discounts: ' . $v['passo'] . '% per friend up to ' . $v['massimo'] . '% plus the review, up to ' . $v['totale'] . '%.'],
        'giudizio-vetrina' => ['Does my guide appear on your website?', 'Only if you join the "Review with a discount" programme, and we decide case by case: from the moment you publish it, your card may appear among "Our hosts\' guides" (on the home page or the "All guides" page), with the property name, the cover, the logo, your first name and the town; your review, separately, may appear in "What they say about us". The card cannot be clicked or searched: no link to the guide, no data about your guests. The discount stays even if we do not publish them.'],
        'giudizio-ritiro' => ['Can I leave the programme?', 'Yes, whenever you like, from Settings → Review with a discount: the card and the review disappear from the home page at once. The discount you already had stays; the one promised on the renewal lapses.'],
        'disdire' => ['Can I cancel?', 'Yes. Turn off automatic renewal from Account & Billing whenever you like: the guide stays online until the end of the period you have already paid for, then goes offline. No lock-in.'],
        'non-rinnovo' => ['What happens if I don\'t renew?', 'At the end of the paid period the guide goes offline by itself. Nothing is deleted: texts, photos and QR code stay saved, and the printed QR code works again as soon as you renew.'],
        'tracciamento' => ['Are guests tracked?', 'No. The guide uses no cookies and doesn\'t appear in search engines. Reading statistics only count anonymous visits: no IP addresses, no profiles.'],
    ];
};
